<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Celebrations and Traditions – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 8th Grade (CEFR: A2.3)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Celebrations and Traditions</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> In This Region, They Have a Custom Of...</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Productive: Write a diary entry about a significant event. Interactive: Respond to peer writing.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can write a diary entry describing a cultural event in a coherent and organized manner (e.g., "Today, I saw a parade for Independence Day. First, the band played music. Then, the floats passed by. Finally, there were fireworks."). Can respond with simple feedback to peer writing about a cultural event (e.g., "I like your story about the festival!"). Can write a short paragraph sharing feelings about a cultural celebration (e.g., "I am excited about celebrating Christmas with my family.").</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification. Activate prior knowledge and introduce the context for writing about celebrations.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher shows a picture of a local celebration (e.g., a parade or a traditional dance). Students brainstorm words related to the image in pairs for 2 minutes. The teacher asks, "What do you see? What do people do? How do they feel?" and writes key vocabulary on the board (e.g., <i>parade, dance, celebrate, festive, enjoy, together</i>).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher writes a simple sentence on the board about the picture, for example: "Last year, people celebrated Independence Day. They marched in a big parade." The teacher models pronunciation, emphasizing word stress in 'celebration' and 'cultural' and the /s/, /z/, /ɪz/ sounds in verbs like 'decorates,' 'gathers,' 'wishes' when appropriate examples arise in student responses or further modeling.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is this a new custom or an old tradition?" (Expected: An old tradition.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Do people celebrate this alone or together?" (Expected: Together.)</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5-7 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Celebrations and Traditions," preparing students for writing.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short diary entry excerpt (2-3 paragraphs) about a cultural celebration, specifically designed to include target grammar (present simple, past simple, gerund after prepositions, present perfect) and vocabulary (e.g., <i>festival, heritage, custom, dance, fireworks, first, next, finally</i>).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Example Diary Entry:</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0; font-style: italic;">"October 28th, Tuesday. Today was amazing! We went to the Folkloric Festival. People have participated in traditional dances and music festivals for years here. First, I saw many traditional masks and costumes. Then, a group was dancing a traditional 'Diablicos' dance. I love watching them! Finally, we enjoyed delicious local cuisine. I am excited about going again next year!"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Describing celebrations and expressing preferences.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist question:</b> "What event is the diary entry about?" (Expected: Folkloric Festival.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> "The writer didn't like the food." (Expected: False.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information matching:</b> Match sequencers (First, Then, Finally) from the text to the events described.</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">8-10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Writing. Students practice target grammar and vocabulary in guided writing activities.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Using Present simple and past simple to describe traditions and events, gerunds after prepositions, Present perfect. Using vocabulary: <i>tradition, custom, parade, celebration, festival, dance, celebrate, enjoy, march, traditional, cultural, national, festive, first, next, finally.</i></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="list-style-type: decimal; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled practice: Sentence Completion.</b> Students complete sentences about traditions using the correct form of verbs (past simple, present simple, gerunds) and appropriate vocabulary.
                        <br>Example: "Panama ___ (celebrate) Independence Day on November 3rd. People are excited about ___ (watch) the parades. They ___ (decorate) their homes with the national flag. Many tourists ___ (have, visit) this festival for years."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled practice: Event Description.</b> The teacher provides a list of events from a hypothetical celebration (e.g., 'see colorful floats,' 'hear traditional music,' 'eat typical food,' 'dance with friends'). Students write 3-4 sentences describing the events of a celebration, using sequencers (<i>First, Then, Finally</i>) and target vocabulary.
                        <br>Example: "Last Saturday, I went to the Parade. First, I saw many colorful floats. Then, I heard traditional music. Finally, I ate some delicious typical food."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pair interaction/Peer Check:</b> Students exchange their written sentences from the previous activity with a partner. They check for correct verb tenses, use of vocabulary, and sequence markers. They give simple feedback, e.g., "I like your use of 'finally'!" or "Check the past tense for 'eat'." The teacher monitors and assists.</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">15-18 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Celebrations and Traditions," focusing on creating a written product.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Individual written product – a diary entry.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Instructions:</b> "Think about a significant cultural event or celebration you have experienced or know about in your community or region. It could be a festival, a national holiday, a special custom, or a family tradition. Write a diary entry (approx. 50-70 words) describing the event, what happened (<i>First, Then, Finally</i>), and how you felt. Use the vocabulary and grammar we practiced (present simple, past simple, gerunds, present perfect)."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Prompt examples:</b> "Today, I saw a parade for Independence Day. First, the band played music. Then, the floats passed by. Finally, there were fireworks. I am excited about celebrating Christmas with my family."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Focus:</b> Students focus on writing a coherent and organized description, expressing feelings, and using target language accurately. The teacher circulates, offering support and encouragement, ensuring students are using sequencers and relevant vocabulary (e.g., <i>parade, celebration, festival, custom, traditional, enjoy</i>).</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">12-15 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy focusing on the writing product and peer interaction.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Peer assessment using a simple feedback checklist.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students exchange their diary entries with a different partner. Each student reads their partner's entry and provides simple written feedback based on a checklist.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Peer Feedback Checklist (students tick or write a short comment):</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: square; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Does the diary entry describe a celebration or custom? (Yes/No)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Are sequencers (<i>First, Then, Finally</i>) used? (Yes/No)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Are new vocabulary words (e.g., <i>parade, festival, traditional</i>) used? (Yes/No)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Is it easy to understand? (Yes/No)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Feedback comment (e.g., "I like your story about the festival!", "Good use of 'finally'.")</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b> Intelligible message, use of target vocabulary (e.g., <i>celebration, tradition, parade, festival</i>), use of sequencers (<i>first, then, finally</i>), clarity of description, and appropriate peer feedback (e.g., "I like your story!").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was one new word or phrase you used in your writing today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was easy/difficult about writing your diary entry?"</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">8-10 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Consolidation of learning and planning for future lessons.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Reflection Prompt:</b>
                <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How has writing about celebrations helped you understand more about your own culture?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one thing you will remember when writing about events in the future?"</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Reflection:</b> The explicit modeling of sentence structure and sequencers was effective. Students were able to apply the past simple and present simple, but some struggled with the correct use of gerunds after prepositions. More controlled practice specifically on gerunds will be needed. The peer assessment activity encouraged interactive writing and provided useful feedback opportunities, with most students providing positive comments. Next time, I will ensure clearer examples for expressing feelings.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson in the theme sequence:</b> In Lesson 5 (Mediation & Integration), students will summarize information about various celebrations and integrate their written descriptions into a short presentation or a collaborative project. They will use their diary entries as a base to explain cultural traditions to others.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5 min</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>